---
// Hidden for now: the leading underscore keeps Astro from building this page. Rename to lab.astro to restore it.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import RobotDemo from '../components/three/RobotDemo.astro';
---

<Base title="Lab" description="Interactive robotics experiments that run entirely in the browser.">
  <div class="container page">
    <header class="narrow-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Lab</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">Interactive experiments</h1>
      <p class="page-lede">Simulations that run entirely in your browser. No server, no install.</p>
    </header>

    <RobotDemo height="clamp(22rem, 60vh, 38rem)" />

    <div class="prose explainer">
      <h2>Rover in an arena</h2>
      <p>
        A small differential-drive robot lives in a walled arena with two pillars, some crates and balls. The physics run
        in <a href="https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/tree/main/wasm">MuJoCo compiled to WebAssembly</a> at 250 Hz,
        rendered with three.js. Click the floor and the rover drives there. Click a crate or ball to kick it.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Sensing.</strong> A lidar on top casts 15 rays across 210°. Rays only see walls and pillars, so the rover
          treats crates and balls as things to push rather than avoid. Red rays are hits.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Steering.</strong> Every 20 ms it picks the free direction closest to its goal, with a small bonus for
          keeping its previous choice so it commits to one side of an obstacle. Speed drops as the way ahead narrows.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Recovery.</strong> If it pushes forward without moving for a second, it backs out while turning. After a
          few failed attempts it gives up on the goal and wanders somewhere else.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The controller is a hand-written reactive policy, not a learned one. Swapping in a trained policy exported to ONNX
        is the natural next experiment.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-top: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5.5rem);
  }

  .narrow-head {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .explainer {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .explainer h2 {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
</style>
